Problem:
Given the quadratic equation about $x$: $x^{2}-(k+1)x+ \frac {1}{4}k^{2}+1=0$, find the value(s) of $k$ according to the following conditions:
1. The product of the two real roots is $5$;
2. The two real roots $x_{1}$, $x_{2}$ satisfy $|x_{1}|=x_{2}$.

Find all real number pairs \((x, y)\) that satisfy:
$$
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
x^{2}+y^{2}+x+y=xy(x+y)-\frac{10}{27}, \\
|xy| \leq \frac{25}{9}.
\end{array}
\right.
$$
